SlothClash core patch 0043: unusable proxy options are ignored, not fatal.

fragment-opts (0032), mux.cool (0039), reality-opts.client-version (0005)
and reality-opts.mlkem-client-fingerprint (0031) failed the whole profile
when a value could not apply: an unknown packets mode, a negative mux.cool
limit, mux.cool on a non-vless proxy or next to a Vision flow, smux or
xdrive, an unknown fingerprint or one without the X25519MLKEM768 key share,
a malformed version. One such node made the core reject a subscription that
stock mihomo, which ignores keys it does not know, loads. Now each is
dropped with a warning in the core log and the proxy loads without it: no
fragmentation, no mux.cool wrapper, the global REALITY client version, the
default ML-KEM handshake. reality-opts.mldsa65-verify stays a config error:
it pins the server, dropping it would weaken the check.

Origin: Rerowros/veles v1.19.34-veles.1 (ff6de754, graceful handling of
Veles proxy keys), as ported to ClashFest (its patch 0040). Delete when the
patches it softens are dropped.

Tests: adapter (fragment-opts and mux.cool load with a warning, the caller's
mapping is not modified, no MuxCool wrapper), adapter/outbound (an invalid
client-version or mlkem-client-fingerprint leaves the field unset and the
fingerprint warning names the reason).

